## Example Use Case

When inserting an order:

```sql
INSERT INTO ORDERS (
    ORDER_ID,
    CUSTOMER_ID,
    AMOUNT,
    CREATED_AT
)
VALUES (
    1001,
    501,
    99.95,
    CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

INSERT INTO OUTBOX_EVENT (
    AGGREGATE_TYPE,
    AGGREGATE_ID,
    EVENT_TYPE,
    PAYLOAD,
    STATUS,
    CREATED_AT
)
VALUES (
    'ORDER',
    '1001',
    'ORDER_CREATED',
    '{"orderId":1001,"customerId":501,"amount":99.95}',
    'NEW',
    CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);
```

Both inserts happen in the same transaction.

If the transaction rolls back, both the order and outbox event are rolled back.

