## Important Oracle Locking Option

For multi-worker processing, Oracle supports this style:

```sql
SELECT *
FROM OUTBOX_EVENT
WHERE STATUS = 'NEW'
ORDER BY CREATED_AT, ID
FETCH FIRST 100 ROWS ONLY
FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
```

However, in many apps, it is easier to first update rows to `PROCESSING`, then read rows assigned to the current worker.

If you run multiple workers, make `worker-id` unique per instance.

For Kubernetes, you can use the pod name as the worker ID.

