## If You Cannot Modify the Business Application

If the business application cannot insert into the outbox table directly, you have two options.

### Option 1: Database Trigger

Create an outbox event automatically when a row is inserted.

```sql
CREATE OR REPLACE TRIGGER TRG_ORDERS_OUTBOX
AFTER INSERT ON ORDERS
FOR EACH ROW
BEGIN
    INSERT INTO OUTBOX_EVENT (
        EVENT_ID,
        AGGREGATE_TYPE,
        AGGREGATE_ID,
        EVENT_TYPE,
        PAYLOAD,
        STATUS,
        CREATED_AT
    )
    VALUES (
        SYS_GUID(),
        'ORDER',
        TO_CHAR(:NEW.ORDER_ID),
        'ORDER_CREATED',
        JSON_OBJECT(
            'orderId' VALUE :NEW.ORDER_ID,
            'customerId' VALUE :NEW.CUSTOMER_ID,
            'amount' VALUE :NEW.AMOUNT
        ),
        'NEW',
        CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
    );
END;
/
```

The trigger runs in the same transaction as the original insert, so it is still transactional.

### Option 2: Separate Polling App

Use the earlier watermark polling approach and write detected changes into an outbox table.

This is less ideal because it can still miss records if the watermark is not designed correctly.

